<topic template="Default" status="Under Construction" modified="2025-04-09T10:20:02.723-04:00" lasteditedby="rbwinst" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../helpproject.xsd">
  <title translate="true">CTP: GWE Constant Temperature Package</title>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1"><text styleclass="Heading1" translate="true">CTP: GWE Constant Temperature Package</text></para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">The </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">CTP: GWE Constant Temperature Package</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> pane is on the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="MODFLOW_Features_Tab" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">MODFLOW Features</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> tab of the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="Object_Properties_Dialog_Box" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Object Properties</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> dialog box.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">The data that can be specified for the CTP package are the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Starting time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">, </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Ending time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">, </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature Active,</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">&#32;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature, Specified Temperature Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true"> and the </text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Chemical Species. </text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">However the species will always be set to &quot;Temperature</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">.&quot; </text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">The </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true"> is the specified temperature at the selected cells for the selected </text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Chemical Species</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> (which is always set to &quot;Temperature&quot;)</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Specified </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Temperature</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Active</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">&quot; can be used to turn on or off a CTP boundary. If the formula for </text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Specified </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Temperature</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Active</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> evaluates to True, a specified temperature boundary will be defined. If it evaluates to False, a specified temperature boundary will not be defined. This can be used to turn on or off specified temperature boundaries at different locations based on a criterion specified by the user. Such a capability can be useful for specifying tidal boundaries where some locations may be alternately flooded or exposed.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> is only used if it has been activated in the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="CTP-GWE-Constant-Temperature-P" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">CTP: GWE Constant Temperature Package</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">. If </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> is specified, the temperature is multiplied by the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Specified Temperature</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> value.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Starting time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> and </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Ending time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> are explained in the help for the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="MODFLOW_Features_Tab" anchor="Times" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">MODFLOW Features</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> tab.</text></para>
  </body>
</topic>
